TOPIC 1 : INTRODUCTION TO DEVOPS
======================================================================

Q1. What is DevOps?

Interview Ready Answer

DevOps is a software development culture and methodology that integrates
the Development and Operations teams to improve collaboration, automate
software delivery, and deliver high-quality software faster and more
reliably.

Definition

DevOps = Development + Operations

It is:
• A culture
• A methodology
• A set of practices

It is NOT:
• A programming language
• A framework
• A software
• A tool

Purpose

• Improve collaboration between Development and Operations teams.
• Automate software development and deployment.
• Deliver software faster and more reliably.
• Reduce manual effort and deployment failures.
• Enable continuous feedback and monitoring.

======================================================================

Q2. Why was DevOps introduced?

Interview Ready Answer

DevOps was introduced to overcome the communication gap between
Development and Operations teams, eliminate manual deployment issues,
reduce release time, automate software delivery, and improve the quality
and reliability of software releases.

Problems Before DevOps

• Development and Operations worked independently.
• Poor communication between teams.
• Manual deployments.
• Slow software releases.
• Environment inconsistencies.
• Frequent deployment failures.
• Delayed bug detection and feedback.

How DevOps Solves These Problems

Development Team
        │
        ▼
Build & Test
        │
        ▼
Continuous Collaboration
        │
        ▼
Operations Team
        │
        ▼
Deployment & Monitoring
        │
        ▼
Continuous Feedback

Benefits

• Better collaboration
• Faster software delivery
• Automated deployment
• Reduced deployment errors
• Faster bug detection
• Improved software quality
• Continuous monitoring
• Continuous feedback

======================================================================

Q3. Is DevOps a Tool, Methodology, or Culture?

Interview Ready Answer

DevOps is a software development culture and methodology. It promotes
collaboration between Development and Operations teams throughout the
software development lifecycle. It also emphasizes automation,
Continuous Integration (CI), Continuous Delivery (CD), monitoring, and
continuous feedback. Tools such as Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, Git, and
Ansible are used to implement DevOps practices.

Key Point

DevOps itself is NOT a tool.

Examples of DevOps Tools

• Jenkins
• Docker
• Kubernetes
• Git
• Ansible
• GitHub Actions
• GitLab CI/CD
• CircleCI

======================================================================
INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Q1. Is DevOps a tool?

Answer:
No. DevOps is a culture and methodology. Tools are used to implement
DevOps practices.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Does DevOps replace the Development or Operations team?

Answer:
No. DevOps does not replace either team. It improves collaboration
between them.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Does DevOps guarantee zero deployment errors?

Answer:
No. DevOps reduces deployment errors through automation and continuous
testing, but it cannot guarantee zero errors.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Is CI/CD the same as DevOps?

Answer:
No. CI/CD is a core practice within DevOps. DevOps is a broader culture
that includes CI/CD, automation, monitoring, collaboration, and
continuous feedback.

